    "token_vs_type": "Type-level rates are point estimates with no CI. A document bootstrap replicate contains only ~63.2% of the distinct documents, so the number of distinct token TYPES it exhibits is driven by the resample's own combinatorics rather than by sampling error in the estimand; a percentile interval around it would be a statement about the bootstrap, not about the slice. Token-level rates are the headline and are CI'd.",
    "tokenization": "the fitted vectorizer's own build_analyzer(); the unigram analyzer is a clone with ngram_range=(1, 1), so lowercasing / token_pattern / preprocessing are byte-for-byte the model's"
  },
